WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:10.314
Hi! Today we'll learn a super quick trick: multiplying and dividing by 10, 100 and 1000.

2
00:00:10.464 --> 00:00:15.138
At the garden shop, one box has 36 flower seeds.

3
00:00:15.288 --> 00:00:23.178
If we buy 100 boxes, how many seeds is that? We don't need to add them one box at a time!

4
00:00:23.328 --> 00:00:30.642
Put 36 in a place value chart. The 3 is in the tens place and the 6 is in the ones place.

5
00:00:30.792 --> 00:00:41.154
When we multiply by 100, every digit moves two places to the left, and we fill the empty places with zeros. We get 3 600.

6
00:00:41.304 --> 00:00:46.986
Times 10 moves one place. Times 1000 moves three places.

7
00:00:47.136 --> 00:00:58.482
Division is the opposite: the digits move to the right. 4 500 divided by 100 moves two places right, and we get 45.

8
00:00:58.632 --> 00:01:03.234
What about times 400? 400 is 4 hundreds.

9
00:01:03.384 --> 00:01:10.386
So for 23 times 400, first work out 23 times 4, which is 92,

10
00:01:10.536 --> 00:01:14.994
then multiply by 100 to get 9 200.

11
00:01:15.144 --> 00:01:23.562
Dividing by 900 works the same way. First divide 7 200 by 100 to get 72,

12
00:01:23.712 --> 00:01:27.690
then divide by 9 to get 8.

13
00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:34.698
One more: each packet has 250 seeds. How many seeds are in 30 packets?

14
00:01:34.848 --> 00:01:41.658
30 is 3 tens. First, 250 times 3 is 750,

15
00:01:41.808 --> 00:01:47.346
then times 10 gives 7 500 seeds.

16
00:01:47.496 --> 00:01:52.818
Watch out! For 40 times 50, many pupils write 200.

17
00:01:52.968 --> 00:02:01.770
4 times 5 is 20, which already ends in a zero. Then we add the two zeros from 40 and 50, so the answer is 2 000.

18
00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:07.794
Multiply the digits first, then count the zeros one by one.

19
00:02:07.944 --> 00:02:17.322
Your turn! What is 56 000 divided by 800? Pause and think.

20
00:02:17.472 --> 00:02:26.562
First divide by 100 to get 560, then divide by 8 to get 70. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:26.712 --> 00:02:36.330
Another one! What is 4 800 divided by 60? Pause and think.

22
00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:44.802
First divide by 10 to get 480, then divide by 6 to get 80. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:44.952 --> 00:02:53.418
Last one! What is 60 times 700? Pause and think.

24
00:02:53.568 --> 00:03:03.546
First, 6 times 7 is 42. Then put three zeros at the end: 42 000. Did you get it right?

25
00:03:03.696 --> 00:03:18.666
Remember: times 10, 100 or 1000 moves the digits one, two or three places left. Division moves them right. For hundreds or thousands, multiply by the front digit first, then move.

26
00:03:18.816 --> 00:03:23.010
Now go and practise in your garden!

